<p>South African President Cyril Ramaphosa has suspended National Police Commissioner Fannie Masemola after Masemola was charged in court over alleged procurement violations tied to a police health services tender reported as worth R332 million to R360 million, or about $20 million to $21 million. Ramaphosa said the move was precautionary and necessary because the police chief plays a central role in fighting crime. The case adds fresh scrutiny to leadership at the South African Police Service. Ramaphosa also named Lieutenant-General Puleng Dimpane, the SAPS divisional commissioner for financial management services, as acting national commissioner. Masemola and his co-accused are due back in court in May.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/ir3ulAoAqAvOrGN3Ef3thR9cLb3DaSaXNgPMGe9nmn0PW9GMtYYoFWEoccJZ9de4Nb9M9h4vV0ourvyciTJWMwF33kvwDNkmz8Qf_SIquaZeX9d8WYUaauE8YOvO6HBNd5YAlTvMKEdwUZ-rfJjp7r55yg2vNc16c9VMa2I4EA' alt='Image accompanying coverage of the suspension of South Africa’s police chief.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Acting leadership: Dimpane previously served as SAPS divisional commissioner for financial management services, putting a senior budget and administration official in temporary charge of the police service.</li><li>Tender value: Outlets variously reported the contract at the center of the case as worth R332 million or R360 million, showing small differences in how they stated the size of the health-services tender.</li><li>What comes next: AllAfrica reported that Masemola is expected to return to court in May alongside co-accused linked to the tender case.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Cyril Ramaphosa: Ramaphosa described the suspension as a precaution tied to the importance of the police commissioner’s office in the national fight against crime, not as a final judgment on the case. (<a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cvglxkjwr5lo'>BBC News</a>)</li><li>South African presidency: The presidency quickly installed Lieutenant-General Puleng Dimpane as acting national commissioner, signaling a focus on continuity in police administration during the legal proceedings. (<a href='https://allafrica.com/stories/202604240069.html'>AllAfrica</a>)</li><li>Media analysis: Al Jazeera placed the decision in a broader anti-corruption and political context, describing it as part of the pressure on Ramaphosa to show action against graft before voters go to the polls. (<a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/4/23/south-africa-president-suspends-police-chief-over-21m-contract'>Al Jazeera</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://abcnews.com/International/wireStory/south-africas-police-chief-suspended-corruption-allegations-132319652'>South Africa&#x27;s police chief suspended over corruption allegations</a> - abcnews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cvglxkjwr5lo'>South African police chief suspended over $20m health contract</a> - bbc.com</li><li><a href='https://allafrica.com/stories/202604240069.html'>South Africa: President Ramaphosa Appoints Acting National Police Commissioner</a> - allafrica.com</li><li><a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/4/23/south-africa-president-suspends-police-chief-over-21m-contract'>South Africa president suspends police chief over $21m contract</a> - aljazeera.com</li><li><a href='https://thepeninsulaqatar.com/article/23/04/2026/south-africa-suspends-police-chief-implicated-in-corruption-case'>South African president Cyril Ramaphosa suspends national police commissioner Fannie Masemola pending investigation into allegations of procurement violations linked to a R332 million (US$20 million) police health services tender.</a> - thepeninsulaqatar.com</li></ul>